ller is  an award-winning food writer and  barbecue competition judge i think if  they can get the cost down  and then do effective promotion to  different communities  i think it could really take off i've  had several  plant-based burgers and they're pretty  good  my son wants to know what's most  important i tell him my job is to look  out for the next generation  beyond meat created a campaign with some  of their celebrity investors including  chris paul and kevin hart and for summer  barbecues  a value pack of beyond burger sales at a  suggested price of  640 per pound narrowing the gap to beef  patties  which are around 5.65 a pound  this cattleman for one isn't buying  everything in here is highly processed  and i think that's my biggest problem  with it  which to you says not as healthy not as  healthy  nothing not even close my father's 86 my  mother's 85.  that's been the staple of their diet for  their entire life  i would like to do as well and follow  right in their footsteps  if you're having animal protein three  times a day and consuming  a lot of processed meat and red meat i  think the literature is pretty clear  on the health implications of that so i  think it would be misguided to say  that that's what's causing their  potential longevity  on the ranch eisley took me for a ride  in his 1928  model a ford almost as old as the ranch  itself  this was the new technology of its time  but brown thinks the model a tells  a different story about his new  technology  henry ford didn't go around saying that  you know the horse is the source of all  evils and wrongs in the world just  created a better way to get from point a  to b  if you think that way you can win  consumers over because they also want  something better  i think beef will continue to sell i  think it will continue to be popular  whether faux meat is a fad or part of a  new normal  as summer continues to sizzle the battle  for your dollars will stretch  from the prairie to the dinner plate for  cbs this morning barry peterson west of  cheyenne wyoming hold on a second barry  gets to ride the classic car  and ride the horse during the story and  you probably and of course turns into a  great story again as usual  yeah it's all about tasting these right  because some of the plant-based burgers  are really bad  right some of them taste better yeah i  actually had my first  vegetarian hot dog last week how was it  oh boy i like the impossible waffle it's  good i'll have to try that one

